    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\nHere's what I implemented for owner soft-delete:\n\n**Entity \u2014 `Owner.java`**\n- Added a persisted `deleted` boolean column (defaults to `false`, so a newly created owner is not deleted) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`.\n\n**Service \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.java`**\n- `deleteOwner(...)` now flags the owner deleted and saves it (retaining the row) instead of removing it.\n- The three create-time duplicate/identity checks now skip deleted owners:\n  - `existsOwnerWithIdentityKey` (hard duplicate / identity key)\n  - `existsOwnerInHousehold` (household duplicate)\n  - `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId` (soft-match)\n\nSo a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**API contract \u2014 `openapi.yml`**\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (MapStruct maps it automatically; `false` for a fresh owner, `true` after delete).\n\n**Schema \u2014 `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`**\n- Added a `deleted` column defaulting to false/`0` NOT NULL to the `owners` table (existing seed inserts omit the column and rely on the default).\n\n`DELETE /api/owners/{id}` still returns 2xx (the controller's existing `204 NO_CONTENT` path is unchanged \u2014 it just now delegates to the soft-delete), and `GET` afterward returns the owner with `deleted: true`.",
