    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this Spring codebase.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** Soft-delete state lives as a plain boolean field on `Owner` with a standard getter/setter and clear javadoc; the delete behavior change lives in `ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner` (swapping `delete` for a flag-and-`save`); and the \"ignore deleted\" concern is applied in exactly the three service methods that back the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks (`existsOwnerWithIdentityKey`, `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId`, `existsOwnerInHousehold`). Nothing leaked into the controller or the model.\n\n- **Scope is correctly bounded.** The other `findAll().stream()` counters (`countOwnersByName`, `countOwnersByCity`, `countOwnersByRegistrationDate`, `countOwnersByHouseholdId`) are intentionally left unfiltered \u2014 they serve namesake/capacity/membership calculations, not the duplicate/identity checks the spec targets. Filtering only the three relevant methods is the right, spec-faithful boundary.\n\n- **Consistent with existing conventions.** This codebase already expresses each rule as an inline `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(...)`; the new `.filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())` is placed uniformly as the leading filter in each method, matching that established idiom rather than introducing a new abstraction. The repetition of that one-liner across three methods is in keeping with the surrounding style, so extracting a helper would stand out more than blend in.\n\n- **Supporting artifacts are complete and consistent.** All four schema dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) add `deleted` with a `NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE/0`, giving the \"newly created owner is false\" guarantee at the DB level, and the OpenAPI schema documents the field as a read-only boolean consistent with the sibling flags.\n\nA maintainer of this repository would find this natural.",
